  {
    "episode_id": 83258,
    "turn_file": "/shared/3/projects/podcasts/transcriptionQueue/turns/pol_appearance_episodes_interviews/8/3/83258.jsonl",
    "turn_idx": 38,
    "turn_text": "Well, the first thing we should do is make sure the $3 trillion we already passed gets implemented out there. The next thing we should do is make sure when the antibodies and the vaccines have all that they need to continue moving forward. We should not be focusing on cannabis or election law or prisoners or others. We should focus on what keeps Americans safe. The virus is here. We did not invite it. We did not ask for it. But we will defeat it together if we work together. But the idea of what the Democrats have done, using this as an opportunity to restructure Congress, so just four and a half percent of Congress can decide what bill gets passed and others, instead of have a reflection of the nation themselves, that everybody has a voice in their government. But this is shutting it down, just why they keep government shut down itself, instead of Congress itself should be working because we are essential. Coming from the USA to every truck driver. that brings the food in or to the doctors or the dispatchers. The Congress won't work, but they will.",
